    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nProbably best illustrated with an example. If I select the last argument or an argument in the middle of the list using `vaa` it gives me this as expected:\r\n![bilde](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ef28eb95-da2b-4ba4-847c-4b7c22034442)\r\n![bilde](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3aa26ab6-5d69-45b8-b47b-ee61c64ec5ce)\r\n\r\nHowever when selecting the first argument:\r\n![bilde](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c737ac7d-9ebe-4da4-babc-7cc009bdaaf4)\r\n\r\nI understand that the selection has to grab the comma in the other direction in this case for it to work, but the problem is that if you use `daa` to delete an argument it, then it works fine in all cases except for the first argument:\r\n![bilde](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fb124cfa-07f0-43d9-9095-9133559f227b)\r\n\r\nAs you can see on the last line, when deleting the first argument it leaves the space that was to the right of the comma.\r\n\r\nAs a fix I sugggest maybe just expanding the text object to include the space as well in this corner case? Kind of like this:\r\n![bilde](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c4b37ee7-36ad-4fa3-9a53-24f0e22ee8de)\r\n\r\nHope that makes sense!\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.10.1 Build type: Release LuaJIT 2.1.1713484068\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. navigate to the first argument of a list\r\n3. type daa to delete the argument\r\n4. observe the extra space\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nI want to be able to delete any argument of an argument list with the quick and simple `daa` without having to fix spacing afterwards.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nI have to fix spacing after deleting the first argument of a list. ",
