            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nI am afraid this is a known limitation of argument textobject which comes from how 'mini.ai' searches for the best target textobject. There are more details in #187 and 551a8726ab382cb02b1e925512162da478ff3811 commit in particular.\r\n\r\nThis can be adjusted via configuring `a` textobject with [`separator` option of `gen_spec.argument()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0a8a1072137d916406507c941698a4bfa9dbbe7a/doc/mini-ai.txt#L641-L649). So the following setup fixes this particular issue (but with caveats described in the `gen_spec.argument` help):\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal ai = require('mini.ai')\r\nai.setup({\r\n  custom_textobjects = {\r\n    a = ai.gen_spec.argument({ separator = '%s*,%s*' }),\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n```",
