            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> * putting the cursor on the whitespace would select the argument to the right of it, the comma following that argument, and the space following that comma (so not the whitespace where the cursor is initially)\r\n\r\nI am afraid this breaks on something like `(aaa  ,  bbb  ,  ccc)`. Although rare in real life, it still needs to be accounted for.\r\nThe current behavior seems to be the best compromise between what is reasonable to expect, various edge cases, and how 'mini.ai' itself works to search for the best textobject region in the current text.",
