        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I understand that you don't really want to change it, but the way it currently behaves it's honestly kind of broken.\r\n> ...\r\n> Wouldn't it be better if it selected the correct arguments even if you have your cursor on a comma, and didn't mess up the formatting, both in regular cases and in edge cases?\r\n\r\nChasing 110% worth of features at the expense of adding more complexity to the code is against overall design of 'mini.nvim'. The current solution has its downsides, but they are the result of a careful compromise.\r\n\r\nAdding an extra `diw` to delete whitespace after an occasional `daa` on the first argument is considered a worthwhile tradeoff here.",
